{
 "name": "poly_inset_nonplanar_divergence",
 "description": "Polygon inset on a NON-PLANAR ring. On a quad whose fourth corner is lifted 0.1 out of the plane of the other three, the reference places each corner of the inset ring on the bent surface (its out-of-plane coordinates come out as 2.1e-5 / 8.443e-3 / 2.1e-5 / 9.1557e-2), while ours come out as 4.24e-3 / 4.24e-3 / 4.24e-3 / 8.7343e-2. Every corner of the inset ring differs, and the difference is almost entirely along the fold axis: in the two in-plane axes the two engines agree to within 2.7e-4, and along the fold axis they part by up to 4.230e-3 at inset 0.12 -- 3.5% of the inset. The second case is the same law on a two-face non-planar base, where all 8 inset-ring corners differ by the same 4.230e-3.",
 "source": "Reference side: headless command-port capture of the inset tool at inset 0.12 (dirty-geometry sweep, task 1123, cases inset_np_one / inset_np_pair_e1). vibe3d side: live drive of this build.",
